                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's very sad that I cannot recommend this game. Saurian had a lot of promise with the dev team's dedication to research to make the dinosaurs as accurate as possible, and it sucks that one person stole a lot of the money and ran with it (I think that's what happened if I remember correctly, but I implore people to double check since it has been a while). \n\nThe game has been met with dead silence for years. The last time they have said anything was January 1st of last year with a dev log. I went to their discord a while back but it was also met with dead silence from the dev team, so I left. I have no idea if they are still working on this game. \n\nOn one hand, I understand that doing consistent dev logs/updates takes time that they would rather spend further working on this game. On the other hand, there has been a deafening silence on their end, to the point where I can't help but question if this game is even still being developed. At the very least, I would appreciate them popping in to tell us they are still here and that they are still working on the game. Maybe a summary of what they have been working on would suffice. Anything to let us know that they are still working on this game.\n\nUntil they start giving consistent updates on Saurian, I cannot recommend anyone getting this game. Like steam says on the page, their last game update was a whole 3 years ago. It's incredibly disappointing that the game went in the direction that it did, and I truly hope we get some sort of update or communication on if the devs are still actively working on this game.\n\nEven if the dev team is no longer working on this game, I would appreciate if they sent a steam post or something announcing that they've stopped development. Again, any communication on what the status of this game is would help a lot.",
